## Component-by-Component Deep Dive

### 1. Server Entry Point — [server.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js)

This is the **brain** of the application at **2,283 lines**. It runs **three servers simultaneously**:

| Server | Port | Protocol | Purpose |
|--------|------|----------|---------|
| Express HTTP | 5001 | REST | Room creation, prompt changes, SMS webhooks, outbound calls |
| WebSocket Voice | 5002 | WS | Twilio phone-call audio streaming |
| WebSocket Chat | 5003 | WS | Text-based chat sessions |

**Key responsibilities:**
- Initializes all service clients (Twilio, Polly, Deepgram, LiveKit)
- Defines Shopify GraphQL functions inline (with external service override pattern)
- Wires up the complete audio processing pipeline
- Handles turn completion, interruption, and multi-channel output routing

---

### 2. Session Management — [session.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/session.js)

The [SessionManager](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/session.js#14-148) class maintains a `Map` of active sessions. Each session is a **rich state object** with ~30 fields tracking:

- **Identity**: `id`, `name`, `phoneNo`, `caller`
- **Audio state**: `isAIResponding`, `currentAudioStream`, `interruption`, `interruptionCooldown`
- **Transcription**: `dgSocket`, `lastTranscript`, `transcriptBuffer`, `currentUserUtterance`
- **VAD state**: `vadProcess`, `ffmpegProcess`, `isVadSpeechActive`, `vadDeepgramBuffer`
- **AI context**: `chatHistory`, `prompt`, `tools`, [messages](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/turn.py#66-80), `lastResponseId`
- **Multi-channel**: `availableChannel[]` (tracks which channels — audio, chat, sms — are active)

**Session lifecycle:**
1. **Create** → Associates with a user from [UserStorage](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/userStore.js#1-147), generates unique ID, builds initial state
2. **Reuse** → If a user already has an active session, it updates and returns the existing one
3. **Cleanup** → Stops audio streams, closes Deepgram socket, kills FFmpeg/VAD processes, clears history

---

### 3. User Storage — [userStore.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/userStore.js)

An **in-memory user database** (not persistent). Each user has: `Name`, `UserId`, [Phone](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/shopify.js#48-64), `Email`, `PastSessionId[]`, `ActiveSessionId`.

- Users can be looked up by **any field** (name, phone, email, session ID)
- Tracks session history via `PastSessionId` array
- Three test users are hardcoded at startup: Shubhanshu, Ankit, Abhinav

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is purely in-memory. All user data is lost on server restart. For production, this would need a database like PostgreSQL (the [pg](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#1570-1659) package is already a dependency).

---

### 4. The Audio Processing Pipeline

This is the most complex part. Here's the complete flow for a **phone call via Twilio**:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Caller
    participant Twilio
    participant WS as WebSocket :5002
    participant FFmpeg
    participant VAD as Silero VAD (Python)
    participant DG as Deepgram STT
    participant Turn as Turn Detector (gRPC)
    participant AI as Gemini LLM
    participant TTS as AWS Polly TTS
    participant Audio as Audio Utils

    User->>Twilio: Speaks
    Twilio->>WS: µ-law audio (base64, 8kHz)
    WS->>FFmpeg: Decode µ-law → PCM s16le
    FFmpeg->>FFmpeg: Resample 8kHz → 16kHz
    FFmpeg->>VAD: PCM 16kHz stream (pipe)
    VAD->>VAD: Detect speech segments
    VAD->>WS: JSON events (speech_start, chunk, speech_end)
    WS->>DG: Speech chunks (linear16)
    DG->>WS: Transcripts (interim + final)
    WS->>Turn: Final transcript + chat history (gRPC)
    Turn->>Turn: SmolLM2 end-of-turn prediction
    Turn->>WS: {end_of_turn: true/false}
    WS->>AI: Complete utterance
    AI->>AI: Gemini processes + tool calls
    AI->>WS: Response text + output_channel
    WS->>TTS: Text → MP3
    TTS->>Audio: MP3 buffer
    Audio->>Audio: MP3 → µ-law (FFmpeg)
    Audio->>Twilio: µ-law chunks (base64)
    Twilio->>User: Hears response
```

#### Audio format conversions:

| Stage | Format | Sample Rate | Encoding |
|-------|--------|-------------|----------|
| Twilio input | µ-law | 8,000 Hz | base64 |
| FFmpeg output | PCM s16le | 16,000 Hz | raw |
| VAD processing | float32 | 16,000 Hz | normalized |
| Deepgram STT | linear16 | 16,000 Hz | raw |
| TTS output | MP3 | varies | compressed |
| Twilio playback | µ-law | 8,000 Hz | base64 |
| LiveKit playback | PCM s16le | 16,000 Hz | AudioFrame |

---

### 5. Voice Activity Detection (VAD) — [vad.py](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/vad.py)

A **Python subprocess** using the **Silero VAD** neural network model (via PyTorch). It runs as a **child process** that communicates via stdin/stdout pipes.

**How it works:**
1. Reads raw PCM audio from stdin
2. Buffers into 250ms chunks (4,000 samples at 16kHz)
3. Runs Silero model inference on each chunk
4. Detects speech segments based on a 0.5 probability threshold
5. Emits JSON events: [speech_start](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/vad.py#137-162), [speech_continue](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/vad.py#163-178), [speech_end](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/vad.py#179-202)
6. Includes prefix/suffix audio buffers for natural speech boundaries
7. Supports CUDA acceleration if available

**Configuration** ([VADConfig](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/vad.py#L13-L30)):
- Minimum speech duration: 100ms
- Minimum silence to end speech: 300ms
- Prefix/suffix duration: 100ms each

---

### 6. Turn Detection — [turn.py](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/turn.py) + [grpc_server.py](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/grpc_server.py)

This is a **custom end-of-turn detector** that determines whether the user has finished speaking their complete thought (not just paused). It uses:

- **Model**: `HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-135M-Instruct` — a tiny 135M param language model
- **Format**: ONNX quantized (int8) for fast CPU inference
- **Method**: Predicts the probability of the `<|im_end|>` token being the next token given the conversation history
- **Threshold**: If P(`<|im_end|>`) > 0.03, the turn is considered complete
- **Transport**: gRPC on port 50051, defined by [turn.proto](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/turn.proto)

**Why this matters**: Instead of using a simple silence timeout (which cuts off people who pause mid-sentence), this ML-based approach understands conversational context. "I want to order..." (pause) will NOT trigger a response, but "I want to order the blue shirt" will.

If the turn detector says "not complete", the system waits 1–2 seconds, then processes anyway as a fallback.

---

### 7. AI Processing — [ai.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/ai.js)

The core LLM integration using **Google Gemini 2.5 Flash Lite**:

1. Maintains a multi-turn `messages[]` conversation with `user` and [model](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/vad.py#48-72) roles
2. Sends the conversation to Gemini with the session's system prompt and tool definitions
3. If Gemini returns **function calls**, executes them against Shopify APIs, then sends results back
4. Parses the response as JSON: `{"response": "...", "output_channel": "audio|chat|sms"}`
5. The `output_channel` lets the AI **choose** how to respond (e.g., user asks "send me an SMS" → AI routes to SMS)

**Supported tools:**

| Tool | Function |
|------|----------|
| [getAllProducts](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#49-111) | Fetch product catalog from Shopify |
| [getUserDetailsByPhoneNo](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/shopify.js#48-64) | Look up customer by phone |
| [getAllOrders](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#155-243) | Get customer's open orders |
| [getOrderById](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#244-342) | Get specific order details |
| [cancelOrder](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#353-432) | Cancel an order with refund/restock |
| `checkOrderCancellable` | Check if order can be cancelled |
| `hangUp` | End the call/connection |

---

### 8. Text-to-Speech (TTS) — Multiple Providers

The system has **three TTS providers** for flexibility:

| Provider | Function | Format | Use |
|----------|----------|--------|-----|
| **AWS Polly** | [synthesizeSpeech3()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#1000-1026) | MP3 | ✅ **Primary** (currently active) |
| **Deepgram Aura-2** | [synthesizeSpeech()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/ai.js#123-135) | MP3 | Available, not primary |
| **Gabber** | [synthesizeSpeech2()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#957-999) | Raw audio | Available, not primary |
| **Deepgram Live TTS** | [synthesizeSpeechStream()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/ai.js#153-180) | PCM linear16 | Streaming (lower latency) |

The streaming TTS from Deepgram is particularly interesting — it streams PCM audio chunks directly to LiveKit in real-time, without waiting for the full audio to be generated.

---

### 9. Audio Utilities — [audio.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/utils/audio.js)

The [universalStreamAudio()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/utils/audio.js#164-193) function is the **smart dispatcher** that handles output regardless of connection type:

```
if connection is WebSocket → Convert MP3 → µ-law → stream to Twilio
if connection is LiveKit Room → Convert MP3 → PCM Int16 → stream via AudioSource
```

**Key features:**
- **Interruption handling**: If the user starts speaking while AI is responding, [handleInterruption()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#1685-1709) immediately stops the audio stream
- **Chunk-based streaming**: Audio is sent in small chunks (~800 samples) with proper timing delays
- **LiveKit integration**: Creates `AudioSource` → `LocalAudioTrack` → publishes to room

---

### 10. Multi-Channel Output — [handleOutput()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#1317-1361) in [server.js:L1317](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#L1317-L1360)

The AI response is routed by `output_channel`:

| Channel | Action |
|---------|--------|
| `audio` | TTS → stream to LiveKit room or Twilio WS |
| [chat](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/turn.py#66-80) | Send JSON text response via WebSocket |
| `sms` | Send via Twilio SMS API |
| `system` | Internal log only |

---

### 11. Shopify Service — [shopify.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/shopify.js)

A clean abstraction over the Shopify Admin GraphQL API (`2025-07` version):
- Centralized [shopifyGraphQL()](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/services/shopify.js#4-29) helper with timeout, error handling, and abort controller
- All CRUD operations: products, customers, orders, cancellation
- The [cancelOrder](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/server.js#353-432) mutation supports refunds, restocking, and customer notification emails

---

### 12. Telephony — [telephony.js](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/telephony.js)

Two functions for Twilio integration:
- **[handleOutboundCall](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/telephony.js#1-20)**: Initiates calls to phone numbers via Twilio API, passing custom parameters (name, prompt, recall URL) in the webhook URL
- **[handleVoiceWebhook](file:///d:/work/ship-fast.studio/Ai-Assistant/modules/telephony.js#21-41)**: Generates TwiML XML to connect the call to the WebSocket voice server, passing caller info and prompt as stream parameters

**Recall URL**: After a call ends, the server POST-s the full conversation history to a configured `recall_url` for logging/analytics.

